From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Timothy Schmidt <timschmidt@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 06:02:05 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: qcom_smbb: keep battery notifications out of
 suspend

With the managed policy active, suspending while the battery charges
failed on the Fx0. The policy's suspend callback inhibits charging, the
fast-charge interrupt then reports the change through
power_supply_changed(), and the battery supply's wakeup source aborts
the transition with "Some devices failed to suspend, or early wake event
detected". A full battery was unaffected because its charger state does
not change.

Register the battery supply without a wakeup source when the charger is
under software control. USB and DC input changes still hold theirs.
---
 drivers/power/supply/qcom_smbb.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_smbb.c b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_smbb.c
index 39ff47bde..3ffd14ef6 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_smbb.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_smbb.c
@@ -1548,6 +1548,12 @@ static int smbb_charger_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 
 	bat_cfg.drv_data = chg;
 	bat_cfg.fwnode = dev_fwnode(&pdev->dev);
+	/*
+	 * Under software control the policy changes the charger state while
+	 * the system suspends; a battery notification must not count as a
+	 * wakeup event then. USB and DC insertion keep their wakeup sources.
+	 */
+	bat_cfg.no_wakeup_source = chg->software_control;
 	chg->bat_psy = devm_power_supply_register(&pdev->dev,
 						  &chg->bat_desc,
 						  &bat_cfg);
